# Who must approve a change, before it can merge, to the files that decide
# what FAM's agents may do (docs/FAM_AGENTS.md, Shared rules, Locked rule
# books; PROBLEMS.md §343, §347). GitHub enforces this only when branch
# protection on Main (and staging) has "Require review from Code Owners" on.
#
# The rule books are signed by the owner, so a changed book already holds its
# agent until it is re-signed. This adds the step before that: nobody merges a
# change to a book, or to the code that checks the signature, without the
# owner's review.

# The rule books, the signed manifest, its signature and the owner's public key.
/docs/agent_rules/                @tjweingart-byte

# Shakespeare's playbook, signed with the rule books.
/docs/journalism_playbook.md      @tjweingart-byte

# The lock that checks the signature, the tool that writes the manifest, and
# the test that keeps unsigned books from shipping.
/agents/rulebooks.py              @tjweingart-byte
/tools/rulebook_manifest.py       @tjweingart-byte
/tests/test_agent_rulebooks.py    @tjweingart-byte

# The byte-for-byte pin the signed hashes depend on, and this file itself.
/.gitattributes                   @tjweingart-byte
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @tjweingart-byte
